commit e7e89ab28153728566668f15a33a5f4595e1b1fb
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 24 19:10:48 2026 +1100

    Read config options where they are used, not at import
    
    objects/base.py, quotasv2.py and quotasv2_detail.py read options at
    import, so any tool that imports them before parsing its
    configuration, such as neutron-ovn-db-sync-util, sees the defaults.
    
    quotasv2 compared the run-time driver with its own import-time value,
    so whether its description said "per project" depended on import
    order. It now checks the driver against QUOTA_DB_DRIVERS, a tuple of
    the two database drivers added to neutron.conf.quota, and
    quotasv2_detail checks the same tuple when its supported check runs.
    
    objects/base.py registered the ORM "SQL execution without transaction"
    listener at import, guarded by "debug" read at import, so the listener
    was silently skipped in any process that imported it before parsing
    its configuration. Registering the listener unconditionally and
    testing "debug" inside it would fix that, but it would also make
    SQLAlchemy build an ORMExecuteState for every ORM statement in every
    process. Instead the listener moves to NeutronDbPluginV2.__init__,
    which already registers listeners this way for the nova notifier and
    runs once the configuration has been parsed, and is registered there
    only when "debug" is set.
    
    This narrows the check to processes that build a core plugin, which is
    enough to monitor Neutron's compliance with SQLAlchemy 2.0, because
    that is where the ORM code runs. neutron-ovn-db-sync-util builds its
    own Ml2Plugin subclass through manager.init(), so it is still covered,
    and now honours "debug" from its configuration file.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    Change-Id: Iebbb77f7b7190126973711100896c0fa1d487570
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

